    "text": "By Patrick ,\n17 hours ago A recent slowdown in corporate income tax and retail sales tax collections has prompted Kansas Gov. Laura Kelly to advise lawmakers to take a more careful approach when shaping the state’s 2026 budget. Despite overall revenues remaining close to projections, the governor warned the Legislature to remain vigilant as economic trends shift. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 15",
